        "id": "daa0c144a096ff958bd9a9d06899e7ad40fbe5a9",
        "tree_id": "8046d3671ce4b89136ff22f74ba37c3b1e00b415",
        "message": "feat(NET-006): wire v3 anim/resync, server hit frames, jitter buffer\n\nA0005 records the Director's 'bypass les limites et go next'. The three\nNET-004 deferrals are folded into this task: a resync frame, a bounded jitter\nbuffer, and a local measurement harness checkpointed as PR-N1. Invariants,\nNET-GATE, Director-only actions and evidence-only are NOT bypassed.\n\nWire v3 adds anim (17 B = the 12-byte core anim_state + entity id and type)\nand resync (10 B) frames. Handshake supports 3..3: a v2 peer is refused, never\nsilently interoperated. All v2 assertions were moved to v3.\n\nThe server validates every anim request with the NET-005 machine and owns hit\nframes from the clip manifest; a client hit claim is ignored (I1/I3/A0001).\nThe presentation jitter buffer adapts between 3 and 8 ticks (100..250 ms,\nD149) and resets on resync — a tunable, not a measured RTT.\n\nThree defects fixed: Room hardcoded the v2 handshake bounds and now reads the\nprotocol range; a jitter test expected growth at a gap the buffer correctly\ntracks; A0005 lacked the D2 headings validate-docs requires.\n\nGDD-ANIM-ARCHITECTURE 0.4 and GDD-NETCODE 0.6 (I9). NET-006's acc repaired to\nthree real test paths; 7 broken accs remain.\n\nAcceptance: anim 5/5, protocol 28/28, combat 7/7, jitter 5/5, full 122/122,\nverify 17/17, typecheck 0, core-math 0, tracer green. No dependency added.\n\nAgent: netcode-engineer\nTask: NET-006",
